# OpenSSH allowed_signers for the Kuzushi local merge-gate receipt.
#
# `scripts/verify-receipt.mjs verify` accepts a receipt signature only from a
# key listed here, under the `kuzushi-verify` signature namespace. Format is one
# entry per line:
#
#   <principal> <keytype> <base64-key>
#
# where <principal> is the signer's git `user.email`. Public keys only — never
# put a private key in this file.
#
# This file is intentionally empty of trusted keys. No signing key is configured
# in this repository yet (`git config gpg.format` and `user.signingkey` are
# unset, and commits on `main` are unsigned), so trusting a key here would be a
# guess, not a fact. Until the owner adds their own key, `verify` refuses every
# receipt and says why.
#
# To trust your key:
#
#   git config gpg.format ssh
#   git config user.signingkey ~/.ssh/<your-key>
#   pnpm verify:receipt:sign            # prints the exact line to paste below
#
# or derive it directly:
#
#   echo "$(git config user.email) $(ssh-keygen -y -f ~/.ssh/<your-key>)" \
#     >> .github/allowed_signers
